# notnet sim — example sudoers rule (issue #339)
#
# The host firewall (defence/host_firewall.sh) needs root to program the
# iptables DOCKER-USER / FORWARD chains, and the parity driver (run_sim.py)
# reads those rules back with `iptables -S`. The sim scripts call sudo with
# `sudo -n` ONLY — they never read a password from the environment or stdin,
# so a NOPASSWD rule is required for the firewall layer to be enforced.
#
# Install (adjust <REPO> to your checkout path):
#
#   sudo install -m 0440 tests/sim/sudoers.example \
#        /etc/sudoers.d/notnet-sim
#
# Scope: exactly two things, nothing else —
#   1. the sim's host_firewall.sh script itself (run as root; it only ever
#      touches iptables rules tagged `notnet-sim` on the 172.29.0.0/16 sim
#      subnet), and
#   2. read-only `iptables -S` used by run_sim.py to verify enforcement.
#
# NEVER grant blanket NOPASSWD for bash/sh, and never export a sudo password
# into the environment (visible in /proc/<pid>/environ to every child,
# including the sim's attack containers).
#
# Replace <REPO> below with the absolute path of your notnet checkout:

dario ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: <REPO>/tests/sim/defence/host_firewall.sh
dario ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/iptables -S DOCKER-USER, \
                           /usr/sbin/iptables -S FORWARD

# Validate before installing:
#   visudo -cf tests/sim/sudoers.example
